+++ b/docs/GARAGE_LIVERY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+# Garage models and livery colors ? 2026-10-10
+
+Requirements: GL01 (actual selected race model), GL02 (editable persistent livery colors), GL03 (future extensibility), GL04 (owner perspective correction), G01/V06/R01/Q01. This owner request replaces the illustrated Garage view; the five existing fictional models and their race geometry remain the source.
+
+The Garage now displays the actual `CarVisual` for Compact, Hauler, Rearsport, Formula and Kart. Dragging the model rotates the menu camera; touching the title area still allows primary menu navigation. The first orthographic preview was rejected for its perspective. The final preview uses restrained perspective, 38? vertical field of view, approximately 17.7? downward angle and model-dependent distances 7.1m/8.5m/4.9m. Gameplay cameras, vehicle dimensions, collisions and canonical simulation are unchanged.
+
+Body and Accent controls recolor the model immediately. Closing the compact color picker saves that car's opaque RGB colors through the existing atomic LocalRecords transaction. The picker provides hue/saturation/value and hex input and fits the 960?540 layout. Reset paint restores that car's authored palette. A failed save restores its last committed colors and presents the existing actionable storage notice. Each car retains independent colors, and driving construction reads the saved livery. Glass, tires, rims, brake lights, headlamps and drivers retain their original materials; shared cream cosmetic/lamp materials were split before batching.
+
+`VehicleLivery` uses a bounded, validated `version:1` document with named `body` and `accent` color slots. The existing LocalRecords schema accepts the new optional `vehicle_liveries` field without changing old record files, timing keys or handling contracts. This is the base for future shape/pattern layers; arbitrary paint placement, texture patterns, decals and cloud cosmetic synchronization are not implemented in this slice. No placeholder customization controls or implementation labels were added to the game.
+
+Changed files: `game/ui/garage_page.gd` (new page), `game/ui/car_showroom.gd`, `game/vehicle/vehicle_livery.gd` (new cosmetic contract), `game/vehicle/car_visual.gd`, `game/vehicle/vehicle_models.gd`, `game/persistence/local_records.gd`, `game/core/app.gd`, the one livery initialization line in `game/core/game.gd`, `game/ui/menu_page_swipe.gd`; `game/tests/test_garage_livery.gd` and three Garage navigation points in `game/tests/test_menu_page_swipe.gd`; this document and status/plan entries. Existing unrelated workspace changes, including concurrent race-world caching, are excluded from the [scoped Git checkpoint](evidence/garage-livery-2026-10-10/scoped-change.patch).
+
+Actual commands used pinned Godot `4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf` through `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1`. Isolated record/library/cloud paths and an empty API URL were used by the Garage test. Normal Windows access was required for Godot certificate/log access after the restricted import failed; no environment permission policy was changed.
